<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William I of Provence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 950–993</span> · Also known as William the Liberator</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William I of Provence, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">the Liberator</a>, was Count of Provence from about 968. In 973 he drove the Saracens from their base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fraxinetum">Fraxinetum</a>, ending decades of raids, and distributed the recovered lands to his followers, becoming effective ruler of the region and founding the first comital dynasty of Provence.</p></div>
